---
import Legal from '../layouts/Legal.astro';

/**
 * Terms (T2.3) — terms of use for the WEBSITE, pre-launch. They deliberately
 * say nothing about licensing, pricing or deployment of the product: all three
 * are undecided (positioning change 2026-08-31) and gate:copy enforces it.
 * The product gets its own terms at launch; this page must not pre-empt them.
 *
 * No governing-law clause yet — there is no registered entity to name one for
 * (owner decision, 2026-10-15). Add it when there is.
 */
---

<Legal
  title="Terms"
  eyebrow="Legal"
  updated="2026-10-15"
  description="The terms for using the Tamtree website and joining the waitlist, before the product launches."
>
  <p class="legal__lead">
    These terms cover your use of the Tamtree website and its waitlist. By using the site you agree
    to them. They are short because, until launch, there is not much to agree to.
  </p>

  <h2>Who we are</h2>
  <p>
    This site is operated by Tamtree (“we”, “us”). You can reach us
    at <a href="mailto:hello@tamtree.io">hello@tamtree.io</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>Tamtree has not launched yet</h2>
  <p>
    This site describes software that is still being built. Features, descriptions, screenshots,
    figures and examples show what we are building and how we intend it to work; they may change
    before launch, and nothing on this site is an offer, a contract, or a promise of a specific
    feature, price or date.
  </p>
  <p>
    Using the Tamtree product, when it is available, will be governed by separate terms that you
    will be asked to accept at that time. These website terms do not grant any licence to the
    product.
  </p>

  <h2>The waitlist</h2>
  <p>
    Joining the waitlist lets us tell you about launch and early access. It does not guarantee
    access, a place in any beta, or particular terms. You can leave at any time with the
    unsubscribe link in any of our emails. How we handle your address is set out in
    our <a href="/privacy/">privacy policy</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>Our content</h2>
  <p>
    The text, graphics, logo and design of this site belong to Tamtree. You are welcome to link to
    any page and to quote short passages, including from our blog posts and their markdown sources,
    as long as you attribute them to Tamtree and link back to the original. Please do not
    republish whole pages or present our content as your own.
  </p>
  <p>
    “Tamtree” and the Tamtree tree mark are our brand. Please do not use them in a way that
    suggests we endorse you or your product.
  </p>

  <h2>Using the site</h2>
  <p>Please do not:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>attempt to break, overload or gain unauthorised access to the site or its infrastructure;</li>
    <li>submit someone else’s email address to the waitlist without their permission;</li>
    <li>use the site to send spam or anything unlawful.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    The site publishes machine-readable versions of its content for people and software alike;
    reading them, including with automated tools, is fine as long as it does not degrade the site
    for others.
  </p>

  <h2>Links to other sites</h2>
  <p>
    We link to other websites where they are useful. We do not control them and are not
    responsible for their content or how they handle your data.
  </p>

  <h2>No warranty</h2>
  <p>
    We work to keep this site accurate and available, but it is provided “as is”, without
    warranties of any kind. To the fullest extent the law allows, we are not liable for any loss
    arising from your use of the site or your reliance on its content. Nothing in these terms
    limits any liability that cannot be limited by law.
  </p>

  <h2>Changes to these terms</h2>
  <p>
    We may update these terms as the site changes. When we do, we will change the date at the top
    of this page; continuing to use the site after that means you accept the updated terms.
  </p>
</Legal>
